{:edb/db-before-t 905 :edb/db-after-t 906 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534218 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:54:09.428Z" 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186166520 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/ea/ea1c45c30bc57d8f04e7bba3e30a33884899fffd0fb712032595ee742a72704c.svg)\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/c3/c3be7834b927a4b8ba684899ee4e617a752ca3f5e09f10a320552fc7f497fb32.svg)\nFind the general solution of the system." 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186166520 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/ea/eaf224db946e02695b83465fa548948a27e7587c7d4b270c604c897cdd4a2228.png)\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/b7/b7ae867ae694152125bc8cdf1ee7ab34c52b0c050408db3d2da86c7cbbc88493.png)\nFind the general solution of the system." 13194139534218 17592186045417 false] [17592186166520 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\mathbf{x}_c(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/6c/6c0f164deb5815fc1c79e3dd724b6725168213938a81089867f4343cb4f05974.svg)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n![](images/5d/5dc5186154c40546a088db1890991e83c6f594d0042866ae9b86cddb3f2d08d8.svg)\nwhere $a,b$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of $\\mathbf{x}_p$ with respect to $t$ gives\n![](images/fa/fad28fb44ef22f703cbc8bd6a07d7d35e4a77ffe4fb3cd0ec5fdd3b107317a1b.svg)\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute $\\mathbf{x}_p$ and $\\mathbf{x}'_p$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 7[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1 \\\\ b-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1=7a \\\\ b-3=7b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nb - 7b = 3\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nb = -\\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n3a - \\dfrac12 - 1 = 7a\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\na = -\\dfrac38.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n![](images/29/29dcb07dde2cdecb330fddb6168319527336ed7a217506727aa6c28241e32a4c.svg)\n\nAnd thus, the general solution is given by\n![](images/3e/3e1b5e881fb3c6d5688fd4978ed0fcc16aec5c6e105c11b919a6a9810762d698.svg)" 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186166520 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\mathbf{x}_c(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/c6/c68bfa253f23fb2c116b8769744e6fd22b7b898047e3ef3fe97f66dd91fefaa1.png)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n![](images/b2/b270d56283fdced6971e1a00fc3e642e379fc9348a0e4fb17a97ba6db2d8fc13.png)\nwhere $a,b$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative