, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-1)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {t}^{2}+(-1)\\cdot t+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-2)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+1\\cdot {t}^{2}+4\\cdot t+(-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186414544 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414536 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186414544 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414538 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186414544 1069 "q-333598" 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186414544 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186414544 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186414544 1072 #uuid "ce5740c3-890f-53a3-a4fc-da96721e3367" 13194139534218 17592186045417 true] [17592186414544 1074 "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2(0)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1 \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1=0 \\\\ {c}_{2}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=-1.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=-1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534218 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-039fd170-03dc-5eb7-83dd-f992ccfbc948" 17592186414498 "answer-0dd1ea2e-80e6-5727-a974-814275f13130" 17592186414499 "answer-16a7977b-7339-57b7-a923-e8d0d8e4ad67" 17592186414500 "answer-170117e4-3734-55f1-8a0e-dfa50d72211d" 17592186414501 "answer-195a8620-7721-5625-905c-f14ca9d8a403" 17592186414502 "answer-21d2e471-2f9a-5c9f-a4df-7096e53f0d75" 17592186414503 "answer-2dcbc6a3-2212-5cc2-8998-578a7cd88408" 17592186414504 "answer-315e3e29-12dd-5d3c-8d68-6a195f6d8f65" 17592186414505 "answer-4757f95f-54fd-51bc-aebf-d567a9828509" 1759218